## 12. CORS not configured

### Risk

No CORS middleware is currently used. That means browsers will apply the same-origin policy by default. This is safer than permissive CORS.

However, if CORS is added later, avoid this dangerous configuration:

```js
app.use(cors({
  origin: '*',
  credentials: true
}));
```

That combination is insecure and often invalid.

### Recommendation

If CORS is needed, restrict it to known origins:

```js
const cors = require('cors');

app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://example.com', 'https://admin.example.com'],
  methods: ['GET'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Authorization', 'Content-Type'],
  credentials: false
}));
```

