Especially if authenticated requests, cookies, or sensitive data are involved.

### Recommendation

If browser clients need CORS, use an allowlist:

```js
const cors = require('cors');

const allowedOrigins = new Set([
  'https://example.com',
  'https://app.example.com',
]);

app.use(cors({
  origin(origin, callback) {
    if (!origin || allowedOrigins.has(origin)) {
