## 13. Missing HTTPS/TLS Enforcement

### Issue

The app itself does not enforce HTTPS. In many deployments, TLS is terminated by a reverse proxy or load balancer, so this may be acceptable. However, sensitive APIs should not be served over plain HTTP in production.

### OWASP Mapping

- OWASP A02: Cryptographic Failures

### Recommendation

Terminate TLS at a trusted proxy and enforce HTTPS.

If behind a proxy:

```js
app.set('trust proxy', 1);

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && !req.secure) {
    return res.redirect(301, `https://${req.headers.host}${req.originalUrl}`);
  }

  next();
});
```

Also configure HSTS via `helmet`:

```js
app.use(helmet.hsts({
  maxAge: 31536000,
  includeSubDomains: true,
  preload: true,
}));
```

Only enable HSTS once HTTPS is confirmed everywhere for the domain.

